From: David Kedves <kedz@kedz.eu>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:02:36 +0200
Subject: Add OSC 8 hyperlink support
Description: Programs like "ls --hyperlink" print OSC 8 hyperlinks, which
 screen silently dropped. Hyperlinks are now stored per cell (a new link id
 plane next to attr/font/colors), so they survive redraws, window switches,
 split regions, copy mode, resizing and reattaching.
 .
 A process wide link table hands out monotonic, never reused ids and is
 garbage collected by mark & sweep over all windows (incl. scrollback)
 and displays. URIs up to 8192 bytes are accepted; control characters
 (C0, DEL, C1, also UTF-8 encoded) are rejected so nothing can be injected
 into the outer terminal. Links are sent with a screen generated id=, so
 pieces of one link drawn separately stay one link.
 .
 Links are only sent to terminals with the new "HL" capability, which is
 set by default for known capable terminal names (xterm*, *-256color,
 kitty*, foot*, ...) and can be forced with "termcapinfo name HL" or
 "termcapinfo name HL@". The new "hyperlinks on|off" command switches the
 feature globally (default on).
 .
 Also: over long OSC strings are now swallowed up to their terminator
 instead of spilling the rest onto the screen.
Author: David Kedves <kedz@kedz.eu>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-29
